# security-baseline tool manifest: the ONE place for versions, assets and sha256.
# install-tools.sh reads it; action.yml and run.sh carry no hash. The docs table
# (docs/components/security-baseline.md) is a copy that test_check.py compares
# with this file.
#
# Columns: tool version platform asset sha256
# Platforms: <linux|darwin>-<amd64|arm64>
#
# Where the hashes come from (re-check them on every version bump):
#   actionlint: rhysd/actionlint release asset actionlint_<version>_checksums.txt
#   zizmor:     the GitHub release asset `digest` field, which zizmor (it publishes no
#               checksum file) gets from GitHub:
#               gh api repos/zizmorcore/zizmor/releases/tags/v<version> --jq '.assets[]|[.name,.digest]|@tsv'
#   Every hash was also cross-checked by downloading the asset and hashing it.
